# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# Build / dist
build/
dist/

# Data.
#
# data/raw/oxfordman/ IS tracked (changed 2026-08-19). The Oxford-Man Realized
# Library was discontinued in 2022 and the only ingestion route left is a Wayback
# snapshot URL that may stop resolving. The primary dependent variable of the
# whole dissertation therefore exists in exactly one place unless it is committed.
# It is ~55 MB, which is a normal size for a repo and a trivial price for the
# alternative.
#
# data/raw/yfinance/GSPC.parquet and VIX.parquet are ALSO tracked (changed
# 2026-08-22, audit vi). They were previously excluded as "re-downloadable", and
# that was wrong for two reasons:
#
#   1. Every model that is not HAR-RV or RW-RV depends on them. GARCH and EGARCH
#      consume `oc_log_return`, which `datasets.build_econometric_frame` builds
#      from the GSPC OHLC; the LSTM family uses the same column; the VIX feeds
#      the LSTM-VIX ablation. Without these two files there is no modelling
#      frame, and `build_econometric_frame` is called BEFORE the
#      `--from-predictions` branch in run_regime_lstm/run_uq -- so even the
#      no-retraining evaluation path dies on a results-only checkout. The
#      Phase-9 gate ("re-run all experiments end-to-end from a fresh checkout")
#      could not pass.
#   2. "Re-downloadable" assumes a live network, a working yfinance, and that
#      the vendor still serves identical history for 2000-2022. None of those is
#      guaranteed for an examiner opening the repo after submission, and any
#      silent revision to the vendor's history would change every result while
#      looking like a reproduction.
#
# They are ~1 MB together. Everything else under yfinance/ (the robustness
# assets, re-pullable and not yet used) plus interim/processed data stays
# ignored: those regenerate deterministically from data/raw.
data/raw/yfinance/**
!data/raw/yfinance/GSPC.parquet
!data/raw/yfinance/VIX.parquet
data/interim/**
data/processed/**
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/interim/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# Results artifacts.
#
# tables/ and predictions/ ARE tracked (changed 2026-08-19). They are small
# (< 2 MB in total), they are the single source of truth for every number cited
# in the dissertation, and until they were committed the roadmap's claim that
# "the committed prediction parquets reproduce the milestone numbers" was not
# literally true -- nothing was committed, so a fresh checkout (the Phase-9
# reproducibility gate) would have regenerated nothing at all. An examiner
# asking "can I reproduce Table 4.2?" must be able to.
#
# figures/ and logs/ stay ignored: figures are large, regenerate deterministically
# from the tracked predictions, and are not cited as evidence.
results/figures/**
results/logs/**
!results/figures/.gitkeep
!results/logs/.gitkeep

# Experiment run dirs.
#
# The resolved-config snapshot of every run IS tracked (changed 2026-08-24,
# audit viii). `snapshot_config` now writes an `_environment` block -- python,
# platform, torch/numpy/pandas/scipy/sklearn/arch/hmmlearn/statsmodels -- into
# each `config.yaml`, and that record is worthless if a fresh checkout cannot
# see it: the whole point is that the interpreter and library set behind every
# committed artefact are auditable from the repo alone. 44 files, ~71 KB.
#
# Note the shape. Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so `experiments/**/run_*/` followed by a negation would silently do
# nothing. Exclude the directory's *contents*, then re-admit the directory and
# the one file worth keeping.
experiments/**/run_*/**
!experiments/**/run_*/
!experiments/**/run_*/config.yaml
runs/

# Model checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.ckpt

